<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert William Wilcox</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1855">1855</a>–<a href="/years/1903">1903</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert William Wilcox was a Native Hawaiian soldier and politician who led armed risings in 1889 against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayonet-constitution">Bayonet Constitution</a> and in January 1895 against the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>, aiming to restore Queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lili-uokalani">Liliʻuokalani</a>. Trained at a military academy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, he was sentenced to death after the 1895 rising, but the sentence was commuted. In 1900 he was elected Hawaii's first delegate to the US Congress.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/robert-william-wilcox.jpg" alt="Robert William Wilcox" width="320" height="405" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Robert_William_Wilcox_1900.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In January 1895 royalists led by <b>Robert Wilcox</b> attempted a counter-revolution, which failed; Liliʻuokalani was arrested, forced to abdicate and imprisoned in ʻIolani Palace.</blockquote><a href="/state/republic-of-hawaii">Republic of Hawaii</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maui">Maui</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-states">the United States</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honolulu">Honolulu</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-states">the United States</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=20.77,-156.27&amp;year=1886" aria-label="Maui on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="345 1395 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Robert William Wilcox"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M795 1665h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M795 1665h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=20.77,-156.27&amp;year=1886">What was here in 1886? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
